/node3/node4","Statically addressed node3 enp8s0 (10.10.1.10/24) and node4 enp8s0 (10.10.2.10/24) via persistent systemd-networkd .network files, each with a static route to the far LAN","Configured VyOS node1: eth1 (10.10.0.1/30 transit), eth2 (10.10.1.254/24 lan-a), static route 10.10.2.0/24 via 10.10.0.2, forward-filter default-drop + established/related accept + tcp/8080 lan-a->lan-b accept, committed and saved","Configured OPNsense node2 via config.xml XML surgery: added opt1 (vtnet1, transit, 10.10.0.2/30) and opt2 (vtnet2, lan-b, 10.10.2.254/24) interfaces, a Gateways gateway_item (GW_LANA via opt1/10.10.0.1), a staticroutes route to 10.10.1.0/24 via GW_LANA, and a filter pass rule for tcp/8080 from 10.10.1.0/24 to 10.10.2.0/24 on opt1; applied via configctl interface reconfigure opt1/opt2 and configctl filter reload","Started a python3 http.server on node4:8080 and verified from node3: HTTP 200 on 8080, ping and tcp/22 refused","Captured baseline boot markers (boot_id for Linux nodes, kern.boottime for FreeBSD node2) on all 4 nodes","Rebooted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (routers first), polling each until exec was available again","Confirmed changed boot_id/kern.boottime on every node post-reboot","Re-verified interface addresses, static routes, and firewall/pf rules persisted across reboot on node1 and node2","Re-verified end-to-end HTTP:8080 reachability and continued blocking of ping/other ports after each reboot, restarting the ephemeral test HTTP server on node4 after its reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node3 can reach node4's HTTP service on tcp/8080","command_ids":["cmd-6171e57e2c0e414e","cmd-e6a750bee3814b5f"],"summary":"curl from node3 to http://10.10.2.10:8080/ returns HTTP:200"},{"requirement":"Other traffic between lan-a and lan-b is refused (default-deny preserved)","command_ids":["cmd-6171e57e2c0e414e","cmd-e6a750bee3814b5f"],"summary":"ping to 10.10.2.10 and nc to tcp/22 and tcp/8081 all fail/timeout while 8080 succeeds"},{"r